(416502, 36489, 9809, '<td valign="top">HA! Great facial expression -- especially the wrinkles on the forehead -- all of it :)<br/> <br/>I like it except I find the sidelighting to be just a bit too harsh. A little fill flash wouldn''t hurt here -- just a little.</td>', 'HA! Great facial expression -- especially the wrinkles on the forehead -- all of it :) I like it except I find the sidelighting to be just a bit too harsh. A little fill flash wouldn''t hurt here -- just a little.', '2003-09-12 04:15:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(416503, 37032, 6172, '<td valign="top">Very nice in every way.  I like the sepia tone, which gives the photo a nostalgic effect.  I like the DOF you used because it deemphasized the background.  Maybe a ribbon?</td>', 'Very nice in every way.  I like the sepia tone, which gives the photo a nostalgic effect.  I like the DOF you used because it deemphasized the background.  Maybe a ribbon?', '2003-09-12 04:16:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(416504, 37119, 6172, '<td valign="top">Sorry to say I don''t see "Nostagia" here at all.</td>', 'Sorry to say I don''t see "Nostagia" here at all.', '2003-09-12 04:17:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(416506, 37224, 9809, '<td valign="top">A bit blurry and noisy and what''s up with the blue specs on the edge of the table? I''m also wondering what the light stripe across the top is all about. Is this a capture from a video camera? Nice idea and interesting vantage point, but the tilt doesn''t seem enough to be on purpose so it just looks crooked.</td>', 'A bit blurry and noisy and what''s up with the blue specs on the edge of the table? I''m also wondering what the light stripe across the top is all about. Is this a capture from a video camera? Nice idea and interesting vantage point, but the tilt doesn''t seem enough to be on purpose so it just looks crooked.', '2003-09-12 04:18:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(416507, 37199, 6172, '<td valign="top">This photo forces me to remember the days when I was a kid (a while back!).  Great shot, excellent use of sepia and the frame is perfect!</td>', 'This photo forces me to remember the days when I was a kid (a while back!).  Great shot, excellent use of sepia and the frame is perfect!', '2003-09-12 04:19:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(416509, 36947, 11405, '<td valign="top">Hey, this picture is my favorite. Nice sepia tone, a litle bit unscharp, great. Composing wonderful. The street, background, ... Congratulations!</td>', 'Hey, this picture is my favorite. Nice sepia tone, a litle bit unscharp, great. Composing wonderful. The street, background, ... Congratulations!', '2003-09-12 04:20:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(416510, 36314, 6172, '<td valign="top">Don''t see any "Nostalgia" here, this looks like any number of playgrounds I see around town now.</td>', 'Don''t see any "Nostalgia" here, this looks like any number of playgrounds I see around town now.', '2003-09-12 04:21:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(416513, 37164, 6172, '<td valign="top">Good subject, cluttered shot.</td>', 'Good subject, cluttered shot.', '2003-09-12 04:22:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(416516, 36999, 6172, '<td valign="top">Yeah, and maybe not all good memories?  Nice shot, good use of a sepia like tone.  The shot does all seem to run together, everything (including the background) is all the same color.</td>', 'Yeah, and maybe not all good memories?  Nice shot, good use of a sepia like tone.  The shot does all seem to run together, everything (including the background) is all the same color.', '2003-09-12 04:24:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(416517, 37233, 6172, '<td valign="top">A little bit too dark for me.  Would be better if the background were not so dark.</td>', 'A little bit too dark for me.  Would be better if the background were not so dark.', '2003-09-12 04:26:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(416518, 36283, 11405, '<td valign="top">Hi, I had problems to decide how you see nostalgia in this picture. So I will only rate the technic. The border between shoes and ground is very sharp. It looks like you had cutted the shoes. The floor is unsharp and is noisy. I little more light would be better. So only 3. Sorry. (also for my english, its long time ago)</td>', 'Hi, I had problems to decide how you see nostalgia in this picture. So I will only rate the technic. The border between shoes and ground is very sharp. It looks like you had cutted the shoes. The floor is unsharp and is noisy. I little more light would be better. So only 3. Sorry. (also for my english, its long time ago)', '2003-09-12 04:28:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(416521, 37136, 6172, '<td valign="top">Great picture - dreadfully terrible title (good thing we don''t vote on them).</td>', 'Great picture - dreadfully terrible title (good thing we don''t vote on them).', '2003-09-12 04:29:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(416524, 36606, 6172, '<td valign="top">Seems like it would be better in a sepia or b&amp;w tone.</td>', 'Seems like it would be better in a sepia or b&w tone.', '2003-09-12 04:31:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(416525, 37072, 11405, '<td valign="top">I kew this toy. My wife is still using the same. So I knew the original colour. This one isn''t grey. Also the colour doesn''t looks like "nostalgia". It is also unsharp. Nice perspective. But only 3</td>', 'I kew this toy. My wife is still using the same. So I knew the original colour. This one isn''t grey. Also the colour doesn''t looks like "nostalgia". It is also unsharp. Nice perspective. But only 3', '2003-09-12 04:31:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(416532, 37119, 8522, '<td valign="top">Shame about the pole to the left of the house and the man on the right, but great otherwise. I find rainbows quite hard to capture this clearly, and I love where it ends in your photo. Your final picture is definitely too small though, and this REALLY needs NeatImage to remove the noise. 6</td>', 'Shame about the pole to the left of the house and the man on the right, but great otherwise. I find rainbows quite hard to capture this clearly, and I love where it ends in your photo. Your final picture is definitely too small though, and this REALLY needs NeatImage to remove the noise. 6', '2003-09-12 04:37:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(416533, 36808, 11405, '<td valign="top">Nice framin and motive. But with "Bring me a dream" I suggested a warm colour for the pic. The grey tone is very hard. Have you tried to take a shot with a sharp needle? I believe it would be better, than the viewer couln''t the LP title and have a dream about his personal music (dream). Perhaps. So only 5</td>', 'Nice framin and motive. But with "Bring me a dream" I suggested a warm colour for the pic. The grey tone is very hard. Have you tried to take a shot with a sharp needle? I believe it would be better, than the viewer couln''t the LP title and have a dream about his personal music (dream). Perhaps. So only 5', '2003-09-12 04:38:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(416536, 37069, 11405, '<td valign="top">Cool. Now I want to drive such a car. Nostalgia pure.</td>', 'Cool. Now I want to drive such a car. Nostalgia pure.', '2003-09-12 04:40:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(416541, 37115, 8522, '<td valign="top">OMG, I''ve taken this exact same picture... it''s Chatsworth House if I''m not mistaken. In my photo, you can tell that the picture at the far end is of Henry VIII. You also seem to have picked up loads of glare. Very hard picture to expose for because of all the lights and shadows. Because of your over-exposure, you''ve lost loads of detail on the bookshelves. The photo could definitely do with sharpening. The composition is a bit boring... one of the shots I tried of this room involved moving to the side more and changing to portrait orientation rather than landscape so I could capture more of the ceiling and floor. I would then have been tempted to crop it so that the far end of the room would be at the bottom of my frame to emphasise the luxuriousness of the ceiling.<br/>I found the entrance hall with the staircase a much more photogenic place... if you take a photo using a column as support, the motion blur on all the tourists is delicious. 5</td>', 'OMG, I''ve taken this exact same picture... it''s Chatsworth House if I''m not mistaken. In my photo, you can tell that the picture at the far end is of Henry VIII. You also seem to have picked up loads of glare. Very hard picture to expose for because of all the lights and shadows. Because of your over-exposure, you''ve lost loads of detail on the bookshelves. The photo could definitely do with sharpening. The composition is a bit boring... one of the shots I tried of this room involved moving to the side more and changing to portrait orientation rather than landscape so I could capture more of the ceiling and floor. I would then have been tempted to crop it so that the far end of the room would be at the bottom of my frame to emphasise the luxuriousness of the ceiling.I found the entrance hall with the staircase a much more photogenic place... if you take a photo using a column as support, the motion blur on all the tourists is delicious. 5', '2003-09-12 04:46:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(416548, 37032, 8522, '<td valign="top">Beautiful car, and I love the low-contrast background with the high-contrast car. As the car is on the side of the photo, it''s a shame it''s not driving into your negative space. I think the picture could have benefited from some sharpening. 6</td>', 'Beautiful car, and I love the low-contrast background with the high-contrast car. As the car is on the side of the photo, it''s a shame it''s not driving into your negative space. I think the picture could have benefited from some sharpening. 6', '2003-09-12 04:52:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(416559, 37050, 8522, '<td valign="top">Intriguing idea, this would have been spot on for me if the foreground person had been a young lad facing the man in tie. Instead, there is a bit of dissonance between the girl and the man in terms of being able to reflect on each other for this to work. I don''t like the post-processing, which is a shame as it almost works. 6</td>', 'Intriguing idea, this would have been spot on for me if the foreground person had been a young lad facing the man in tie. Instead, there is a bit of dissonance between the girl and the man in terms of being able to reflect on each other for this to work. I don''t like the post-processing, which is a shame as it almost works. 6', '2003-09-12 05:00:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(416562, 37203, 8522, '<td valign="top">I don''t like the way your background horizon cuts through the camera. The placement of the photo doesn''t quite work for me either. The camera is too centred in the frame for my taste. Could do with some sharpening. Nice sepia toning though. 6</td>', 'I don''t like the way your background horizon cuts through the camera. The placement of the photo doesn''t quite work for me either. The camera is too centred in the frame for my taste. Could do with some sharpening. Nice sepia toning though. 6', '2003-09-12 05:02:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(416565, 36989, 10635, '<td valign="top">I like this shot, you can imagine them thinking of times gone by.</td>', 'I like this shot, you can imagine them thinking of times gone by.', '2003-09-12 05:03:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(416567, 36362, 10635, '<td valign="top">I like this, the paint on the buses is very interesting.  I cant make up my mind though as to whether I would have shown to tops of the buses as well,</td>', 'I like this, the paint on the buses is very interesting.  I cant make up my mind though as to whether I would have shown to tops of the buses as well,', '2003-09-12 05:05:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(416568, 37212, 8522, '<td valign="top">Lovely idea, but for this to take me back, I think I''d need to see it from the child''s point of view which is difficult from this overbearing vantage point. I''d have been tempted to get to his height or lower. The selective desaturation leaves me puzzled... I can''t see what it''s trying to achieve. I''d have prefered complete b&amp;w. The composition is a little odd... are his feet in the centre of the frame because that''s where you want my eye to focus first? I naturally want to look at his head first which is right at the top of the frame. IMO, the eye is more comfortable if the focal point is in the centre 3rd. 6<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-09-17 09:48:46.</i></td>', 'Lovely idea, but for this to take me back, I think I''d need to see it from the child''s point of view which is difficult from this overbearing vantage point. I''d have been tempted to get to his height or lower. The selective desaturation leaves me puzzled... I can''t see what it''s trying to achieve. I''d have prefered complete b&w. The composition is a little odd... are his feet in the centre of the frame because that''s where you want my eye to focus first? I naturally want to look at his head first which is right at the top of the frame. IMO, the eye is more comfortable if the focal point is in the centre 3rd. 6', '2003-09-12 05:06:52.000000', '2003-09-17 10:48:46.000000', 1),
(416573, 36812, 8522, '<td valign="top">It doesn''t look as if the subject is looking at the photo, it''s too tilted. A real shame about the ugly shadows from the glasses frames. I think I''d have liked a much tighter crop, and following the top-left to bottom-right diagonal so he is looking down to the right. The first self portrait is great! I would have knocked out a lot of the extreme shadows in PS to make the background appear black. 6</td>', 'It doesn''t look as if the subject is looking at the photo, it''s too tilted. A real shame about the ugly shadows from the glasses frames. I think I''d have liked a much tighter crop, and following the top-left to bottom-right diagonal so he is looking down to the right. The first self portrait is great! I would have knocked out a lot of the extreme shadows in PS to make the background appear black. 6', '2003-09-12 05:19:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(416574, 36553, 7301, '<td valign="top">Great idea, maybe a slight improvement would have been to have the same area of doorway and step showing in both photos but worth a 10 anyway</td>', 'Great idea, maybe a slight improvement would have been to have the same area of doorway and step showing in both photos but worth a 10 anyway', '2003-09-12 05:19:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(416576, 37102, 8522, '<td valign="top">Very amusing. Bed wetting was a nice touch!<br/>Nicely lit. Composition is unusual, but effective. 7</td>', 'Very amusing. Bed wetting was a nice touch!Nicely lit. Composition is unusual, but effective. 7', '2003-09-12 05:20:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(416582, 36362, 6172, '<td valign="top">If these buses weren''t in a junk yard you would have a better message.</td>', 'If these buses weren''t in a junk yard you would have a better message.', '2003-09-12 05:27:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(416583, 37059, 8522, '<td valign="top">Exisiting artwork!! And poor contrast, unimaginative composition. 1</td>', 'Exisiting artwork!! And poor contrast, unimaginative composition. 1', '2003-09-12 05:27:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(416584, 36813, 6172, '<td valign="top">She is rather attractive!  She has that space out look though.</td>', 'She is rather attractive!  She has that space out look though.', '2003-09-12 05:28:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(416586, 37150, 6172, '<td valign="top">One of the better shots I''ve seen so far.</td>', 'One of the better shots I''ve seen so far.', '2003-09-12 05:29:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(416588, 36479, 6172, '<td valign="top">A dead breed</td>', 'A dead breed', '2003-09-12 05:32:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(416590, 37199, 8522, '<td valign="top">Normally I can''t stand these borders, but it is appropriate here and works well. Very nice sepia toning, a little different to the usual kind but very effective. Lovely textures, the tree is particularly nice. The tyres are a nice touch. Great composition. Gorgeous lighting and exposure. 8</td>', 'Normally I can''t stand these borders, but it is appropriate here and works well. Very nice sepia toning, a little different to the usual kind but very effective. Lovely textures, the tree is particularly nice. The tyres are a nice touch. Great composition. Gorgeous lighting and exposure. 8', '2003-09-12 05:34:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(416591, 36412, 8522, '<td valign="top">Picture is far too small, and I don''t know how this is supposed to take me back in time. 2</td>', 'Picture is far too small, and I don''t know how this is supposed to take me back in time. 2', '2003-09-12 05:34:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(416593, 37139, 8522, '<td valign="top">I''m a bit baffled as to why there''s so much negative space. My eye doesn''t know where it''s supposed to focus. 4</td>', 'I''m a bit baffled as to why there''s so much negative space. My eye doesn''t know where it''s supposed to focus. 4', '2003-09-12 05:35:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(416594, 36746, 6172, '<td valign="top">The color version of this photo doesn''t invoke as many nostalgic feelings as a b&amp;w version would.  Great focus and composition here.</td>', 'The color version of this photo doesn''t invoke as many nostalgic feelings as a b&w version would.  Great focus and composition here.', '2003-09-12 05:36:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(416595, 36447, 8522, '<td valign="top">Why the selective desaturation? I can''t understand what it''s trying to achieve. Nice composition though, the foreground light works well. 6</td>', 'Why the selective desaturation? I can''t understand what it''s trying to achieve. Nice composition though, the foreground light works well. 6', '2003-09-12 05:39:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(416596, 36860, 11811, '<td valign="top">very nice shot.</td>', 'very nice shot.', '2003-09-12 05:39:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(416597, 37148, 11811, '<td valign="top">excellent</td>', 'excellent', '2003-09-12 05:40:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(416599, 37131, 11811, '<td valign="top">excellent</td>', 'excellent', '2003-09-12 05:41:51.000000', NULL, 1);
