(418545, 37158, 669, '<td valign="top">Composition: Interesting that you left a lot of the background in.  Think I might have made it a little squarer.<br/>Technical: The lighting position/shadows are good, but it seems a little dark, meaning noise is a little high.  You also seem to have over-sharpened; the right hand side has a white line.<br/>Meets challenge: Yes<br/>Overall impression: Good effort.<br/> <br/>[ If this style of comment is useful, please leave a few yourself!  www.calcaria.net/dpc.html ]</td>', 'Composition: Interesting that you left a lot of the background in.  Think I might have made it a little squarer.Technical: The lighting position/shadows are good, but it seems a little dark, meaning noise is a little high.  You also seem to have over-sharpened; the right hand side has a white line.Meets challenge: YesOverall impression: Good effort. [ If this style of comment is useful, please leave a few yourself!  www.calcaria.net/dpc.html ]', '2003-09-14 07:27:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(418548, 37151, 669, '<td valign="top">Composition: Interesting angle of shot.  Could do with rotating a few degrees counter-clockwise.<br/>Technical: The over-exposed sky draws the eye quite a lot.  The whole pic is in focus, so you could have focused high up on the building so the camera thinks "oh, it''s bright", then drag the camera down with the button half pressed.  This would mean the sky isn''t so white.  Otherwise, the colouring is quite nice.<br/>Meets challenge: Mostly.<br/>Overall impression: Good effort.  Practice with exposure will help a lot.<br/> <br/>[ If this style of comment is useful, please leave a few yourself!  www.calcaria.net/dpc.html ]</td>', 'Composition: Interesting angle of shot.  Could do with rotating a few degrees counter-clockwise.Technical: The over-exposed sky draws the eye quite a lot.  The whole pic is in focus, so you could have focused high up on the building so the camera thinks "oh, it''s bright", then drag the camera down with the button half pressed.  This would mean the sky isn''t so white.  Otherwise, the colouring is quite nice.Meets challenge: Mostly.Overall impression: Good effort.  Practice with exposure will help a lot. [ If this style of comment is useful, please leave a few yourself!  www.calcaria.net/dpc.html ]', '2003-09-14 07:34:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(418551, 36813, 669, '<td valign="top">Composition: I would have preferred the subject more in the left of the frame, possibly more upright.<br/>Technical: Excellent colourisation and lighting.  The border looks ok, but I can''t help thinking it would look the same with a solid colour outside the white line.<br/>Meets challenge: Ish<br/>Overall impression: Nice soft focus, very well done, but not sure about the composition.<br/> <br/>[ If this style of comment is useful, please leave a few yourself!  www.calcaria.net/dpc.html ]</td>', 'Composition: I would have preferred the subject more in the left of the frame, possibly more upright.Technical: Excellent colourisation and lighting.  The border looks ok, but I can''t help thinking it would look the same with a solid colour outside the white line.Meets challenge: IshOverall impression: Nice soft focus, very well done, but not sure about the composition. [ If this style of comment is useful, please leave a few yourself!  www.calcaria.net/dpc.html ]', '2003-09-14 07:39:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(418555, 37139, 669, '<td valign="top">Composition: Would have preferred the subject more in the centre of the image, and larger if poss.<br/>Technical: Nice use of leading lines and nice coloursiation.  It looks like it could be rotated a little CCW?<br/>Meets challenge: Yes<br/>Overall impression: I think I''d have gone for a more sombre title, but nice idea.<br/> <br/>[ If this style of comment is useful, please leave a few yourself!  www.calcaria.net/dpc.html ]</td>', 'Composition: Would have preferred the subject more in the centre of the image, and larger if poss.Technical: Nice use of leading lines and nice coloursiation.  It looks like it could be rotated a little CCW?Meets challenge: YesOverall impression: I think I''d have gone for a more sombre title, but nice idea. [ If this style of comment is useful, please leave a few yourself!  www.calcaria.net/dpc.html ]', '2003-09-14 07:42:58.000000', NULL, 1),
